lla, CA 92093-0112. Email: sspiro@ucsd.edu\\n\\nFirst published: 24 September 2018\\n\\nhttps://doi.org/10.1002/jgt.22401Digital Object Identifier (DOI)\\n\\nRead the full text\\n\\n  * References\\n\\n### Abstract\\n\\nWe derive a correspondence between the eigenvalues of the adjacency matrix Image: urn:x-wiley:03649024:media:jgt22401:jgt22401-math-0001 and the signless Laplacian matrix Image: urn:x-wiley:03649024:media:jgt22401:jgt22401-math-0002 of a graph Image: urn:x-wiley:03649024:media:jgt22401:jgt22401-math-0003 when Image: urn:x-wiley:03649024:media:jgt22401:jgt22401-math-0004 is Image: urn:x-wiley:03649024:media:jgt22401:jgt22401-math-0005-biregular by using the relation Image: urn:x-wiley:03649024:media:jgt22401:jgt22401-math-0006. This motivates asking when it is possible to have Image: urn:x-wiley:03649024:media:jgt22401:jgt22401-math-0007 for Image: urn:x-wiley:03649024:media:jgt22401:jgt22401-math-0008 a polynomial, Image: urn:x-wiley:03649024:media:jgt22401:jgt22401-math-0009, and Image: urn:x-wiley:03649024:media:jgt22401:jgt22401-math-0010 matrices associated to a graph Image: urn:x-wiley:03649024:media:jgt22401:jgt22401-math-0011. It turns out that, essentially, this can only happen if Image: urn:x-wiley:03649024:media:jgt22401:jgt22401-math-0012 is either regular or biregular.\\n\\nREFERENCES\\n\\n  * 1 A. E. Brouwer and W. H. Haemers, Spectra of Graphs, Springer Science & Business Media (2011).\\n\\nGoogle Scholar\\n\\n  * 2 S. Butler and F. Chung, Spectral graph Theory, Handbook of Linear Algebra (2006), 47.\\n\\nGoogle Scholar\\n\\n  * 3 D. Cvetković and S. K. Simić, Towards a spectral theory of graphs based on the signless laplacian, II, Linear Algebra and its Applications 432 (2010), 2257–2272.\\n\\nWeb of Science® Google Scholar\\n\\n  * 4 R. P. Stanley, Variations on differential posets, Institute for Mathematics and Its Applications 19 (1990), 145.\\n\\nGoogle Scholar\\n\\n  * 5 R. P. Stanley, Algebraic Combinatorics, Springer, New York (